www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/48.html",{"type":45,"ref":46,"location":49},"provenance",{"_":47,"target":48},"Tyros, Greece","https://www.geonames.org/256631/nisi-naxos.html",{"geo":50},"37.07257,25.48616",{"_":52,"ref":53}," Petrographic imagery at ",{"_":54,"target":54},"https://iiif.csad.ox.ac.uk/viewer/isicily/ISic000804","",{"layout":57},{"p":58,"rs":59,"damage":55},"The Latin text is engraved over two lines (letters c.20 mm high, but of uneven height), to a maximum length of 52 cm.",{"_":60,"ana":61,"ref":62},"chiselled","#execution.chiselled","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1",{"lettering":64,"dimensions":65}," The letters show some irregularity, with fairly pronounced serifs, and lengthy tails to the letter R. The first two words are separated from the rest by a space; an interpunct is visible at the end of the dedicant’s name, and the final abbreviated phrase is separated from the rest by a large hedera (ivy leaf). The letter I in line 1 is frequently taller than the rest (but so too is the first L in line 1); the final I of line 1 is somewhat irregularly carved.",[66,74,80],{"type":67,"l":68,"from":69,"to":69,"h":70,"unit":71,"atLeast":72,"atMost":73},"letterHeight","Line 1","line1","18-25","mm","18","25",{"type":67,"l":75,"from":76,"to":76,"h":77,"unit":71,"atLeast":78,"atMost":79},"Line 2","line2","19-23","19","23",{"type":81,"l":82,"from":69,"to":76,"h":83,"unit":71,"atLeast":84,"atMost":85},"interlinear","Interlineation lines 1-2","7-15","7","15",{"_":87,"notBefore":88,"notAfter":89,"evidence":90},"Statue can be dated stylistically to the late Antonine period (i.e. the 180s or 190s CE), and the text is compatible with such a date.",180,199,"context",[92,97],{"_":93,"type":94,"ref":95,"region":96},"Halaesa","ancient","http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462225","Sicilia",{"_":98,"type":99,"ref":100,"offset":101,"region":96},"Castel di Tusa","modern","http://sws.geonames.org/2525099","near",[103],[104,105],37.99907,14.26197,[107,108],37.9